# hooks and gates

**Read [`memory/hooks-and-gates.md`](../memory/hooks-and-gates.md) before going further.** This rule exists to
fire on the topic and send you there; the knowledge itself lives in one place, not two.

**Why it is worth the read:** Enforcement here fails OPEN, by three separate routes, and a hook that never loaded looks exactly like a hook that correctly allowed everything. Nothing in the source says which of those you are looking at.

## Before you touch anything

- Run `node hooks/status.js`. It separates never-ran / live / stale / disabled, which is the distinction the symptom does not give you.
- If a gate is not firing, restart the host before debugging. Hook config is read at startup and a gate registered mid-session enforces nothing, silently.
- Never match a raw absolute `file_path`. Relativise against `cwd` first -- `toProjectPath` in `hooks/lib/gates.js`.

